inflation and ImageView: honour what the app's own classes decide

Four places where an AOSP guarantee an app class relies on was missing
(measured on Instagram 455), plus two default-off diagnostics.

1. TypedArray.getNonResourceString returned null for everything; AOSP returns
   an immediate XML string. CornerPunchedImageView requires one and threw
   "Required value was null."; LayoutInflater substituted a FrameLayout and
   ReelAvatarWithBadgeView then died on a ClassCastException.

2. TypedArray.getResourceId / getString read 0 / the literal text for the
   numeric reference spelling `@0x7f131764` that BinaryXmlParser emits when the
   target id has no name in the table (Instagram's strings live in its own
   language pack). FittingTextView threw "textId has invalid value".

3. LayoutInflater.buildLayoutParams walked the element's layout_* attributes
   onto whatever parent.generateLayoutParams(attrs) returned, overwriting an
   APP override that deliberately ignores them (MACAPK_GENLP_APP_FINAL, default
   on). Material's TabLayout returns generateDefaultLayoutParams(); the profile
   tab views are declared layout_width="0px" + weight, so each measured 0 px
   wide and the grid / reels / tagged icons never drew. ViewGroup.LayoutParams
   gains a package-private flag set by the (int, int) constructor to tell a
   size chosen in code from one read from attributes.

4. ImageView shrank the drawable's BOUNDS for a scaling scaleType; AOSP keeps
   the native size and scales through a matrix. Applied to drawables the APK
   defines (MACAPK_IMAGEVIEW_APP_MATRIX, default on): Instagram's vector class
   positions its glyph by gravity inside the bounds, so a 24 dp glyph in a
   12 dp view showed one corner.

Diagnostics: MACAPK_TRACE_RRECT=1 (each distinct Canvas.drawRoundRect, for a
view that paints its own chrome in onDraw) and MACAPK_TRACE_SETLP=<class>
(every setLayoutParams on that view class, with the caller).

Applies to vendor/macapk at 57c9912 with `patch -p1` from vendor/macapk.

